{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "והקהל את העדה", :translit "ve-hak'hel et ha-edah", :gloss "and assemble the congregation"} {:he "אלו הטהורים הגדולים שבעדה", :translit "elu ha-tehorim ha-gedolim she-va-edah", :gloss "these are the pure ones, the great ones of the congregation"} {:he "ולא עשה כן", :translit "ve-lo asah khen", :gloss "and he did not do so"} {:he "ויקהילו משה ואהרן את הקהל", :translit "va-yakhilu moshe ve-aharon et ha-kahal", :gloss "and Moses and Aaron assembled the congregation"} {:he "גדולים וקטנים", :translit "gedolim u-ketanim", :gloss "great and small"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between God's command in Numbers 20:8 and its execution in Numbers 20:10 — Moses assembled everyone, not only the elite"}], :frame {:text "The phrase \"והקהל\" with the definite article can be read as singling out a specific group — the distinguished members of the congregation. The parallel verse Numbers 20:10 records the actual gathering with \"הקהל,\" which the Ba'al HaTurim reads as the entire assembly. The midrashic method of reading nuance into the choice between \"העדה\" and \"הקהל\" appears in Rashi on Numbers 20:10, who cites the tradition that Moses assembled everyone on that day.", :sources ["Rashi on Numbers 20:10"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Contrast between God's command in Numbers 20:8 and its execution in Numbers 20:10 — Moses assembled everyone, not only the elite", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :numbers, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:30:09.425409888Z", :model "glm-5.2"}